  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Cedar County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Skip to content\n \n\n \n\n Cedar County, Iowa\n Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n \n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nCedar County Elections\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nWelcome to our Elections Website!\n The Election Department in the Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find information on past elections or upcoming elections.\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nElected Officials\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n \n\n 2026 General\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Results By Precinct · Unofficial Results\n Results Summary · Unofficial Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n4\n \n \n\n 2025 City/School Election\n City/School Election\n \n\n More Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nI registered as an independent; why does my card say \"NP\" or \"No Party\"?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nIowa does not recognize an “independent” party. Instead, “No Party” is used to indicate a lack of affiliation with a political party. \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nCan I vote for someone that is not on the ballot?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. For each race on the ballot, a line is provided for you to write-in the name of someone for whom you wish to vote for. Make sure you color in the oval! \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Cedar County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated October 1, 2026\n \n\n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n5,094\n \n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n4,669\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n3,097\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n102\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 12,962\n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Cedar County Auditor\n\n Cedar County Courthouse\n \n400 Cedar Street\n \nTipton, IA 52772\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00AM to 4:00PM\n \nMonday - Friday \n \nPhone Numbers\n\n Office: (563) 886-3168\n \nFax: (563) 866-3339 \n \n\n \n\n Contact Cedar County Elections\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
